begin{aligned}x+y+z & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivative of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+y+z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function ${f}_{z}(x,y,z)$ is defined only for \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of ${f}_{z}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{z}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $z$ exists on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}\\cap {(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321085 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321086 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321087 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321088 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321089 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1041 "selection" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321087 13194139534937 true] [17592186321084 1110 #uuid "ccf78f1b-49bd-59f9-8276-4dac4e64921a" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321085 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z=0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321085 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321085 1111 #uuid "98e1d76a-95fd-5cff-89a7-935c66a0a7dd" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321086 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\le 0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321086 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321086 1111 #uuid "60e3fcd2-0b47-5157-a6fa-9b0311a2bfa6" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321087 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321087 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321087 11