] [17592186321091 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321094 13194139534937 true] [17592186321091 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321095 13194139534937 true] [17592186321091 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321096 13194139534937 true] [17592186321091 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534937 true] [17592186321091 1041 "selection" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321091 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321096 13194139534937 true] [17592186321091 1110 #uuid "1b3c09a2-0ac1-5598-9123-353925213644" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321092 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ne z}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321092 1111 #uuid "3148eab3-0b75-5775-b738-357a4c594f3a" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321093 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\ge z}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321093 1111 #uuid "4015b873-b9f8-5e03-a4d1-e7d7ae607e9a" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321094 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy\\le z}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321094 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321094 1111 #uuid "7cf4b8fa-dce1-573a-bec6-8289db3723ae" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321095 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy<z}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321095 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321095 1111 #uuid "92514a59-50a3-5ba2-86e9-f65555809f1e" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321096 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,xy>z}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321096 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321096 1111 #uuid "77ab28e6-bd9c-5b47-a808-34967eb13c9e" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321097 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321098 13194139534937 true] [17592186321097 1089 "q-72005" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321097 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534937 true] [17592186321097 1100 "Given that $g(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂g}{∂x}=\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂g}{∂y}=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y)$ where all partial derivatives of $g$ exist." 13194139534937 true] [17592186321097 1113 #uuid "ed7bcfe5-c1ea-56d9-b1e4-351fef6e9306" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321097 1145 "First, notice that $g(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ is defined only when ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0.$ So, the domain of $g$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{g}={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${g}_{x}(x,y)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ is defined only when ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0.$ So, the domain of ${g}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{g}_{x}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}.\n$$\n\n- The function ${g}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ is defined only when ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${g}_{y}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{g}_{y}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $g$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{g}\\cap {D}_{{g}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{g}_{y}} & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}>0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321099 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321100 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321101 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321102 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321103 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1041 "selection" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321102 13194139534937 true] [17592186321098 1110 #uuid "ea54a922-cd8d-5604-8b3d-e3c059805f1e" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321099 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321099 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321099 1111 #uuid "4a5e107b-3f50-