g}_{y}(x,y)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}{e}^{x/y}}{{y}^{2}}$ is defined only when $x\\ge 0$ and $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${g}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{g}_{y}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,y\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $g$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{g}\\cap {D}_{{g}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{g}_{y}} & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,y\\ne 0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,x>0,y\\ne 0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,y\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,x>0,y\\ne 0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321106 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321107 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321108 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321109 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321110 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1041 "selection" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321106 13194139534937 true] [17592186321105 1110 #uuid "f30ecd9d-bb53-5315-933c-e7c026c37751" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321106 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,x>0,y\\ne 0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321106 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321106 1111 #uuid "ea5cff9a-aae1-5f98-9b2f-4632f52d422e" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321107 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,x=0,y\\ne 0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321107 1111 #uuid "f923fac3-f4d2-5047-b3f4-41b9e7fad34d" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321108 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,x>0,y>0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321108 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321108 1111 #uuid "1d37609d-2ab7-5894-8b99-06eb1b65babd" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321109 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,y\\ne 0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321109 1111 #uuid "8bee1b94-cbc2-5f5c-814a-7e785113db2d" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321110 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\ge 0,y>0}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321110 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321110 1111 #uuid "8d5e0a5e-1dec-5ee0-b6c9-f1535238339c" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321111 1017 #edb/ref 17592186321112 13194139534937 true] [17592186321111 1089 "q-72022" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321111 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534937 true] [17592186321111 1100 "Which of the following statements are true about the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy(z-1))?$\n\n- The partial derivative with respect to $z$ is defined at $(3,2,1)$\n- ${f}_{y}(1,1,2)$ is defined\n- ${f}_{x}(1,2,3)$ is defined" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321111 1113 #uuid "929098a3-e3fe-5fb1-aaac-1e50c43eff3d" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321111 1145 "First, we compute the partial derivatives of $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{1}{xy(z-1)}\\cdot y(z-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{1}{xy(z-1)}\\cdot x(z-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{y} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{1}{xy(z-1)}\\cdot xy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{z-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's examine the statements one-by-one.  \n\n- Statement I is false. If we substitute $(3,2,1)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(3,2,1)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot 2\\cdot (1-1))=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0),\n$$\n\nwhich is undefined.\n\n- Statement II is true. If we substitute $(1,1,2)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(1,1,2)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 1\\cdot (2-1))=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)=0,\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{y}$ is also defined at $(1,1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,1,2) & =\\frac{1}{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. If we substitute $(1,2,3)$ into $f$, we get\n\n$$\nf(1,2,3)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1\\cdot 2\\cdot (3-1))=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4),\n$$\n\nand ${f}_{x}$ is also defined at $(1,2,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,2,3) & =\\frac{1}{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II and III  only'." 13194139534937 true] [175921863211