$(x,y,z)$ on which all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." 13194139534937 true] [17592186321118 1113 #uuid "735926a2-d3a9-5db6-a4eb-54bb660a7efe" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321118 1145 "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x+y+z)$ is defined for any $x$, $y$, and $z.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}=\\frac{1}{1+(x+y+z)^{2}}$ is defined for any $x$, $y$, and $z.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )}.\n$$\n\n- Similarly, the domains of ${f}_{y}$ and ${f}_{z}$ are\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={D}_{{f}_{z}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the partial derivatives of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}} \\\\  & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )}\\cap {(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )} \\\\  & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321120 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321121 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321122 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321123 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1000 #edb/ref 17592186321124 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1041 "selection" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1104 #edb/ref 17592186321123 13194139534937 true] [17592186321119 1110 #uuid "d58194a7-e7d3-5ca0-ae88-f9905cc9f289" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321120 1034 "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\ne 1}" 13194139534937 true] [17592186321120 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534937 true] [17592186321120 1111 #uuid "b751beaf-5c3b-5a76-b629-23e9e15e36aa" 13194139534